 ProcessDoubleQuotes←{
⍝ Replaces pairs of double quotes by ⍺ (a ⎕R transformation string) and removes the escape character from `\"`.
⍝ A `\"` with a preceding (opening) `"` closes that pair: its `\` is not an escape character.
⍝ Code, links, images with special attributes and HTML tags are left alone.
     quotes←⍺
     html←⍵
     (2>≡html)∧~'"'∊html:html           ⍝ Without any double quote there is nothing to do (and that's the common case)
     bbt←'`[^`].*?`'                    ⍝ Between back-ticks (= code)
     cdq←'"".+?""'                      ⍝ Catch what is enclosed between two pairs (that is four of them!) of double quotes
     cim←'!\[[^\)].*?\){.*?}'           ⍝ Catch image with special attributes
     cl1←'\[\]\([^)]*.?\)'              ⍝ Catch simple link
     cl2←'\[[^]]*.?\]\([^)]*.?\)'       ⍝ Catch simple link
     ced←'\\"'                          ⍝ Catch escaped double quote
     ctag←'<[^>]*?>'                    ⍝ Catch opening HTML tag
     cpb←'&amp;pointybracket_open([^&]*.?)&amp;pointybracket_close' ⍝ Catch pointy brackets
     me←'\0'
     pair←'"(.*?)"'
     cpb cl1 cl2 cim bbt cdq ctag ced pair ⎕R((7⍴⊂me),'"'quotes)⍠('Mode' 'D')('DotAll' 1)⊣html
 }
